A||||5||FAXKID||CHECK ENGINE LIGHT||||1||
Z||000000||FAXKID||08-10-2001||11:31 PM||||My check engine light has been coming on for years now,but most of the time it pops on after I have driven for a while.I don't know if it has to reach a certain temp or something else.However lately when I first start the car the check engine light comes on right then and if it does it runs very rough and sometimes the engine will even quit running.If I restart it,and the light does not come on it runs fine.Anyone ever had this happen?By the way its a 86 gt six.||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||08-10-2001||11:39 PM||||Take off the black cover over the cig lighter...you'll see the "black box" to check the codes. Use a paper clip or any other piece of metal (or wire) and jumper the bottom right two ("pass side") w/ the key in the on position (but not to the start position)....the check engine light will go "flash...........flash flash" three times..then it'll flash again, but itll be the code to tell what the prob is (ex. "flash flash flash........flash flash" = 32)...check the haynes or chiltons manual to see what the code is.<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="red"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||DRH||08-10-2001||11:47 PM||||The ECM (computer) has self diagnostics and stores a "code" almost any time it lights the Service Engine light. Look in the first link below for a description of the codes and how to get them. You might want to come back here and post what they were before you buy any parts. Sometimes the codes are a little misleading about what is actually wrong. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/codes.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg/codes.html</A> <P>Also, the main menu to the same site has a TON of info on Fieros.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.mindspring.com/~fierosketch/osg</A> <P>Good luck!<P>Edited to add:<P>Hey My 7 Fieros, you posted while I was off hunting links  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><p>[This message has been edited by DRH (edited 08-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||fieroburton||08-25-2001||11:23 AM||||just did it this is what i got before it started to repeat itself<BR>*__**<BR>*__**<BR>*__**<BR>*__***<BR>*__***<BR>*__***<BR>*__**<BR>*__**<BR>*__**<BR>what does this mean ?<BR>ps that was easy  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000004||starfighter007@msn.com||08-25-2001||11:37 AM||||You are showing a code 13 that is your oxegen sensor(o-2) circuit I would check to make sure your O-2 is plugged in If so go get a new sensor install it reset your computer by disconnecting your battery for a couple minutes. then go out for a drive this should solve your prob. Let us know what happens. <p>[This message has been edited by starfighter007@msn.com (edited 08-25-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||maryjane||08-25-2001||03:43 PM||||The guys posting above gave you correct info.<BR>I repeat tho, if you don't have a repair manual of some sort, get one. Or get 2 and keep one in the Fiero always. They rarely break down in your driveway. Make sure you coat the threads on the new 02 sensor with anti-seize and don't overtighten it. I believe the setting is 30ft lbs. (don't quote me on that) You can crack the bore it threads into. Also makes it easier to change next time. Don't be surprised if your car runs rough for the first few miles after changin the 02. ECMs need to reset and can't do it sitting in the drive. If you still have problems, try archive search and The Ogre's cave. Lot's of info on sensors in both.||||reg||1
